       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,600 mg/day of ibuprofen is three times the maximum labeled daily dose, and 2,400 mg per dose is three times the usual single-dose ceiling. I know of no indication that supports it. The risk of serious harm is high, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and seizures. A normal baseline kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg PO QID (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO TID (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO QID (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), with a note about GI protection and monitoring renal function\n\nIf you're treating a specific condition and need more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than these give, I'd suggest a pharmacy or clinical pharmacology consult. Adding a different agent might work better than escalating ibuprofen.\n\nIf the order is something you still want to place, you'd need to enter it directly through your institution's override process. I'm not able to submit it for you."
